--- body ---
`erg -h` / `erg --help` / `erg help` currently uses `<arg>` angle-bracket
notation for required arguments (e.g. `close <id|file> <reason> [dir]`).
These render as HTML entities (`&lt;`, `&gt;`) when captured and displayed
in web/conversation contexts, making the output hard to read.

There is also no regression test: when a new command was added to the
`switch` in `main.go` without being added to `printUsage()`, the omission
went undetected until a user ran the command and got "Unknown command".

**Desired behaviour:**

Replace angle-bracket notation with UPPER_CASE for required positional
arguments in `printUsage()`:

```
  validate FILES...         Validate individual .erg files (format, headers, refs)
  check [DIR]               Corpus-level checks (duplicate IDs, cycles, refs)
  ready [DIR] [--json]      Show tickets ready for work
  next-id [DIR]             Print the next available ticket ID
  new TITLE [DIR]           Create a new ticket file atomically
  close ID REASON [DIR]     Close a ticket atomically
  log ID LINE [DIR]         Append a timestamped log entry to a ticket
  archive [ID...] [DIR]     Move closed tickets to tickets/closed/
  migrate [DIR]             Convert legacy Status: headers to Closed: form
  init [DIR]                Bootstrap tickets/ support files from embedded assets
  uninstall [DIR]           Remove files/fragments managed by `erg init`
  version                   Print version, path, build date, and obsolescence info
  update                    Fetch and replace binary from origin
```

Optional args stay in `[brackets]`. Required args become UPPER_CASE.

**Tests (TDD first):**

Add `tests/test_help.sh`:

- `erg -h` exits 0 and prints to stderr — PASS/FAIL
- `erg --help` exits 0 — PASS/FAIL
- `erg help` exits 0 — PASS/FAIL
- For each command name in the canonical list (validate check ready next-id
  new close log archive migrate init uninstall version update): assert the
  name appears in `erg -h` output — one PASS/FAIL per command
- No `<` or `>` characters appear in the output — PASS/FAIL

Wire `test_help` into `TEST_SUITES` in the Makefile.

**Implementation notes:**

- Edit `printUsage()` in `tickets/tools/go/main.go` only.
- The package-level doc comment (lines 4–18) uses the Go `godoc` convention
  with angle brackets; leave it unchanged — it is not user-facing output.
- The `version` description should be updated to reflect the new
  structured output added in PR #68: path, hash, build date, OS/arch.
- No other files need changing.
